  {
    "name": "read_memory",
    "description": "Reads all of user memory and all of this trip's memory. Returns how many items each holds, and the most it can hold. Then every item, in the order added, with its ID, whether it's user or trip memory, and its text.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {},
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "annotations": {
      "readOnlyHint": true
    },
    "execution": {
      "taskSupport": "forbidden"
    },
    "_meta": {
      "anthropic/alwaysLoad": true
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "add_memory_item",
    "description": "Adds an item to user memory or to this trip's memory. Each holds at most 50 items. The reply gives the new item's ID.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "memory": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "user",
            "trip"
          ]
        },
        "text": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Plain text, at most 300 characters."
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "memory",
        "text"
      ],
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "execution": {
      "taskSupport": "forbidden"
    },
    "_meta": {
      "anthropic/alwaysLoad": true
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "update_memory_item",
    "description": "Replaces a memory item's text. The item keeps its ID, and stays in the same memory.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "itemId": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "A memory item ID, such as mem_k7m2x9qa."
        },
        "text": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Plain text, at most 300 characters."
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "itemId",
        "text"
      ],
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "execution": {
      "taskSupport": "forbidden"
    },
    "_meta": {
      "anthropic/alwaysLoad": true
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "forget_memory_item",
    "description": "Removes a memory item for good.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "itemId": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "A memory item ID, such as mem_k7m2x9qa."
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "itemId"
      ],
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "additionalProperties": false
    },
    "execution": {
      "taskSupport": "forbidden"
    },
    "_meta": {
      "anthropic/alwaysLoad": true
    }
  }
]
```

### What they return

User A's session makes each call, except the add of "Posh hotels only.", which is user B's, in another session. User A then tries to change and forget that item, `mem_nkxtyzbn`.

